1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,998
You get paid. Two weeks later,

2
00:00:01,898 --> 00:00:03,063
the money is just...

3
00:00:02,963 --> 00:00:05,247
gone. And you have no idea where it went.

4
00:00:05,497 --> 00:00:07,632
Sound familiar? You're not bad with money.

5
00:00:07,532 --> 00:00:09,280
You just don't have a plan for it.

6
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:11,481
One simple rule fixes this.

7
00:00:11,381 --> 00:00:12,990
Fifty. Thirty. Twenty.

8
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:14,520
By the end of this video,

9
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,984
you'll know your three numbers,

10
00:00:15,884 --> 00:00:16,881
down to the dollar.

11
00:00:17,131 --> 00:00:19,391
Here's the idea. You split your take-home

12
00:00:19,291 --> 00:00:20,602
pay into three buckets.

13
00:00:20,852 --> 00:00:22,448
Fifty percent goes to needs.

14
00:00:22,348 --> 00:00:24,586
The stuff you must pay to live and work.

15
00:00:24,836 --> 00:00:26,501
Thirty percent goes to wants.

16
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:28,821
The fun stuff that makes life worth living.

17
00:00:29,071 --> 00:00:31,254
And twenty percent goes to your future.

18
00:00:31,154 --> 00:00:32,964
Savings, and crushing your debt.

19
00:00:33,214 --> 00:00:35,309
It was made popular by Elizabeth Warren

20
00:00:35,209 --> 00:00:36,537
and her daughter Amelia,

21
00:00:36,437 --> 00:00:38,020
in their book All Your Worth.

22
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:40,614
Step one. Start with your take-home pay.

23
00:00:40,514 --> 00:00:41,512
Not your salary.

24
00:00:41,762 --> 00:00:43,875
It's what actually lands in your bank

25
00:00:43,775 --> 00:00:44,963
account after taxes.

26
00:00:45,213 --> 00:00:47,200
If retirement money comes out of your

27
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:49,546
paycheck, count it toward your twenty percent.

28
00:00:49,796 --> 00:00:50,805
Let's make it real.

29
00:00:50,705 --> 00:00:53,198
Say you bring home three thousand dollars a month.

30
00:00:53,448 --> 00:00:55,491
Fifteen hundred dollars goes to needs.

31
00:00:55,741 --> 00:00:57,627
Nine hundred dollars goes to wants.

32
00:00:57,877 --> 00:01:00,154
And six hundred dollars goes to savings

33
00:01:00,054 --> 00:01:01,494
and extra debt payments.

34
00:01:01,744 --> 00:01:03,241
That's it. Three numbers.

35
00:01:03,141 --> 00:01:04,918
Every single dollar has a job.

36
00:01:05,168 --> 00:01:07,031
Needs are the bills you'd still pay,

37
00:01:06,931 --> 00:01:08,255
even in your worst month.

38
00:01:08,505 --> 00:01:11,629
Rent or mortgage. Utilities. Basic groceries.

39
00:01:11,879 --> 00:01:13,824
Getting to work. A car payment,

40
00:01:13,724 --> 00:01:14,955
gas, or a bus pass.

41
00:01:15,205 --> 00:01:17,964
Insurance, child care, and the minimum payment

42
00:01:17,864 --> 00:01:18,773
on every debt.

43
00:01:19,023 --> 00:01:21,227
But careful! Groceries are a need.

44
00:01:21,127 --> 00:01:22,155
Takeout is NOT.

45
00:01:22,405 --> 00:01:24,741
Wants are everything that's nice to have,

46
00:01:24,641 --> 00:01:25,668
but not required.

47
00:01:25,918 --> 00:01:28,017
Eating out. Streaming. New clothes.

48
00:01:27,917 --> 00:01:29,787
Concerts. That shiny new phone.

49
00:01:30,037 --> 00:01:31,481
And here's the best part.

50
00:01:31,381 --> 00:01:33,846
This money is meant to be spent. Guilt free!

51
00:01:34,096 --> 00:01:36,357
Because a budget you actually enjoy is

52
00:01:36,257 --> 00:01:38,291
a budget you'll actually stick to.

53
00:01:38,541 --> 00:01:40,893
The last twenty percent is for future you.

54
00:01:41,143 --> 00:01:43,341
First, build a small emergency fund,

55
00:01:43,241 --> 00:01:45,381
so surprises don't become new debt.

56
00:01:45,631 --> 00:01:47,543
Next, attack high interest debt,

57
00:01:47,443 --> 00:01:48,562
like credit cards.

58
00:01:48,812 --> 00:01:51,445
Then, save for retirement and your bigger goals.

59
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:53,165
Now the eye opening part.

60
00:01:53,065 --> 00:01:55,576
Compare the plan with what you really spend.

61
00:01:55,826 --> 00:01:57,337
Pull up your last two or three

62
00:01:57,237 --> 00:01:58,984
months of bank and card statements.

63
00:01:59,234 --> 00:02:01,269
Sort every purchase into needs,

64
00:02:01,169 --> 00:02:02,392
wants, or savings.

65
00:02:02,642 --> 00:02:04,215
Most people are shocked.

66
00:02:04,115 --> 00:02:06,486
Wants hide in tiny, everyday charges.

67
00:02:06,736 --> 00:02:08,414
But what if your needs eat way

68
00:02:08,314 --> 00:02:10,307
more than half? This is the question

69
00:02:10,207 --> 00:02:10,886
I get most.

70
00:02:11,136 --> 00:02:13,015
Honestly? That's really common,

71
00:02:12,915 --> 00:02:15,426
especially with high rent or a low income.

72
00:02:15,676 --> 00:02:17,204
It doesn't mean you failed.

73
00:02:17,104 --> 00:02:18,631
These numbers are a target,

74
00:02:18,531 --> 00:02:19,159
not a law.

75
00:02:19,409 --> 00:02:21,856
Try sixty, twenty, twenty for a while.

76
00:02:21,756 --> 00:02:23,647
Or even seventy, twenty, ten.

77
00:02:23,897 --> 00:02:25,321
The one thing to protect?

78
00:02:25,221 --> 00:02:27,176
Save something. Even if it's small.

79
00:02:27,426 --> 00:02:28,899
Then chip away at your needs,

80
00:02:28,799 --> 00:02:29,704
little by little.

81
00:02:29,954 --> 00:02:32,249
Shop around for car and renters insurance

82
00:02:32,149 --> 00:02:32,891
once a year.

83
00:02:33,141 --> 00:02:35,112
Check a cheaper prepaid phone plan.

84
00:02:35,012 --> 00:02:37,304
Many cost way less than the big carriers.

85
00:02:37,554 --> 00:02:38,637
Cook at home more.

86
00:02:38,537 --> 00:02:40,385
Buy store brands for the basics.

87
00:02:40,635 --> 00:02:41,964
And when your lease is up,

88
00:02:41,864 --> 00:02:43,949
think about a roommate or a cheaper place.

89
00:02:44,199 --> 00:02:46,824
The secret to sticking with it? Automate everything.

90
00:02:47,074 --> 00:02:49,086
On payday, move your twenty percent to

91
00:02:48,986 --> 00:02:50,695
savings before you can touch it.

92
00:02:50,945 --> 00:02:52,368
Put your bills on autopay,

93
00:02:52,268 --> 00:02:54,045
so your needs are always covered.

94
00:02:54,295 --> 00:02:55,817
Whatever's left in checking?

95
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,543
That's your wants money. Enjoy it!

96
00:02:57,793 --> 00:02:59,658
Watch out for three mistakes.

97
00:02:59,558 --> 00:03:01,849
One: using your salary before taxes.

98
00:03:01,749 --> 00:03:03,675
Your numbers come out too big.

99
00:03:03,925 --> 00:03:05,763
Two: calling every want a need.

100
00:03:05,663 --> 00:03:07,109
Be honest with yourself.

101
00:03:07,359 --> 00:03:09,684
Three: forgetting costs that hit once or

102
00:03:09,584 --> 00:03:11,964
twice a year, like car repairs and gifts.

103
00:03:12,214 --> 00:03:13,611
Divide those by twelve,

104
00:03:13,511 --> 00:03:15,754
and set that amount aside every month.

105
00:03:16,004 --> 00:03:18,253
Quick recap. Find your take-home pay.

106
00:03:18,153 --> 00:03:20,054
Split it fifty, thirty, twenty.

107
00:03:20,304 --> 00:03:21,840
Check your real spending,

108
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:23,276
adjust if needs run high,

109
00:03:23,176 --> 00:03:24,769
and automate your savings.

110
00:03:25,019 --> 00:03:26,683
You don't need a fancy app or

111
00:03:26,583 --> 00:03:29,056
a finance degree. Just three simple numbers.

112
00:03:29,306 --> 00:03:31,717
If your twenty percent starts at zero,

113
00:03:31,617 --> 00:03:33,845
watch my emergency fund video next.

114
00:03:34,095 --> 00:03:36,357
Subscribe for one simple money move every

115
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,203
day. And tell me your three numbers

116
00:03:38,103 --> 00:03:39,047
in the comments!
